/P 486 0 R
/E (We would need to make sure that when a voter casts their ballot, the vote is immediately encrypted on the voter's device using a public key provided by the election authority. This public key will only able to encrypt data. Each vote can be signed by the voter's private key \(or through an authentication method\) to ensure the vote's authenticity and prevent tampering or double voting.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
